From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:01:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: reorder RX frames when WED does not handle RX

mt76_rx_poll_complete() skips mt76_rx_aggr_reorder() whenever
mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) is true. However, MT7622 WED v1
only offloads TX: mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(&dev->mmio.wed) returns false, the
RX DMA rings stay host-managed, and mt7915_mcu_init_firmware() queries
MCU_WA_PARAM_CMD(CAPABILITY) rather than configuring WED RX offload.

On MT7622 with an MT7915 card and mt7915e wed_enable=1, 5 GHz Block Ack
frames reach mt76_rx_poll_complete() unreordered whenever WED is
attached. Out-of-order MPDUs therefore hit mt76_check_ccmp_pn() with
IV < last PN and are marked RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR. On a 160 MHz AX client
upload benchmark on MT7622 + MT7915 with WED v1 active, debug counters
recorded 2171 single and 5661 A-MSDU 802.3 frames falsely marked as PN
replays (out of 228603 total passed frames) with out-of-order BA
sequence numbers visible in kernel logs, while with WED detached they
dropped to 7 single and 0 A-MSDU marks. Once mt76 frees
RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR 802.3 frames in mt76_rx_complete() (commit
3115dbc9eedf ("wifi: mt76: free a replayed 802.3 frame with all its
subframes")), 5 GHz client upload throughput collapses from ~840 Mbit/s
to ~109-123 Mbit/s with ~7000 TCP retransmissions per 15 s run.

Only bypass mt76_rx_aggr_reorder() for WED when
mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(&dev->mmio.wed) is also true. This matches the
predicate already used by mt7915 and mt7996 for RX offload setup and
keeps the bypass intact on MT7986 (WED v2 with WO) and MT7988/MT7996
(WED v3 with HWRRO) where WED/firmware handles RX reordering, as well as
for mt76_npu_device_active(dev).
---
 mac80211.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index c981475f..a4b21011 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1658,7 +1658,8 @@ void mt76_rx_poll_complete(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id q,
 
 	while ((skb = __skb_dequeue(&dev->rx_skb[q])) != NULL) {
 		mt76_check_sta(dev, skb);
-		if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) ||
+		if ((mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) &&
+		     mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(&dev->mmio.wed)) ||
 		    mt76_npu_device_active(dev))
 			__skb_queue_tail(&frames, skb);
 		else
